{
  "title": "Aneurysmal Bone Cyst",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8036/aneurysmal-bone-cyst",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 8 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Aneurysmal Bone Cysts are benign, non-neoplastic, reactive bone lesions that most commonly occur in the femur and tibia. The condition typically presents in patients less than 20 years of age with focal pain and swelling.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs showing an expansile, eccentric, and lytic lesion with bony septae and a biopsy showing blood-filled spaces without endothelial lining.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually nonoperative for lesions associated with a fracture. Aggressive curettage, with adjuvant treatment and bone grafting, is indicated for symptomatic lesions without associated fracture.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "75% of patients are **< 20 yrs.**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "15% in spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": ">60% in long bones (Femur and tibia being most common)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "51% occured in the lower extremities, 22.5% in upper extremities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually in metaphysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "metatarsal and calcaneus are the most common locations in the foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior elements of pelvis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be found in similar location as telangiectatic osteosarcomas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary and secondary forms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "primary ABC",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "driven by upregulation of the **ubiquitin-specific protease USP6** (TRE17-USP6when combined by a translocation with a promoter pairing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "most commonly described translocation TRE17-USP6",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "secondary ABC",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "not considered a neoplasm because no known translocation has been identified",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**associated with other tumors** 30% of time",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "giant cell tumor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chondroblastoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fibrous dysplasia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chondromyxoid fibroma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "NOF",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain** and **swelling**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**may present with pathologic fracture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "neurologic deficits possible with spine lesions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8036/images/Case%20E%20-%20femur%20-%20xray%20-%20parsons_moved.gif",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8036/images/Case%20C%20-%20calc%20-%20xray%20-%20parsons_moved.png",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**expansile, eccentric** and **lytic** lesion with **bony septae** (\"bubbly appearance\")",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually in metaphyseal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "classic cases have **thin rim of periosteal new bone** surrounding lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "no matrix mineralization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI or CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "will show **multiple fluid lines**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8036/images/Case%20C%20-%20calc%20-%20MRI%20b%20-%20parsons_moved.gif",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lesion can expand into soft tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
